"use strict";

const PATHWAY_DESCRIPTIONS = {
  "Aerospace & Defence Engineering": `Aerospace and Defence Engineering is the design, build and testing of aircraft, spacecraft, satellites and defence systems. Engineers work on structures, propulsion, aerodynamics, avionics and the integration of them into systems that must perform under extreme conditions. Its purpose is to move people, information and capability safely through the air and beyond, where the cost of failure is high.`,
  "Chemical & Process Engineering": `Chemical and Process Engineering is about designing and running the processes that turn raw materials into useful products at scale, from fuels and medicines to food, water and materials. Engineers design equipment, optimise reactions and keep processes safe, efficient and increasingly sustainable. Its purpose is to convert scientific know how into large scale production that society depends on every day.`,
  "Forensic Science": `Forensic Science is about applying science to investigate crime, analysing evidence such as DNA, chemicals, fibres, traces and digital data to support the justice system. Practitioners carry out careful laboratory and scene work and often present findings as expert witnesses. Its purpose is to bring scientific rigour to criminal investigation, so that evidence can be trusted in court.`,
  "Diagnostics, Imaging & Clinical Support": `Diagnostics, Imaging and Clinical Support is the science and technology behind diagnosing illness, from medical imaging and laboratory testing to measuring how the body is working. Practitioners operate specialist equipment, run investigations and produce the evidence clinicians rely on. Its purpose is to give doctors and patients the accurate information they need to diagnose, monitor and treat disease.`,
  "Occupational & Organisational Psychology": `Occupational and Organisational Psychology is about applying psychology to work and organisations, improving how people are selected, developed, led and supported. Practitioners work on assessment, wellbeing, leadership, performance and change. Its purpose is to make workplaces both more effective and better for the people in them.`,
  "Secondary Teaching": `Secondary Teaching is the work of teaching a subject to young people aged roughly eleven to eighteen, planning lessons, assessing progress and supporting them through a formative stage of life. Teachers combine deep subject knowledge with classroom skill and pastoral care. Its purpose is to help each generation gain the knowledge, qualifications and confidence to shape their own futures.`,
  "Higher Education & Academic Research": `Higher Education and Academic Research is about advancing knowledge through research and teaching at universities and research institutes. Academics design and run studies, publish findings, and often teach and supervise students. Its purpose is to create new understanding and pass it on, extending the frontier of a discipline while training the next generation within it.`,
  "Solicitor Practice": `Solicitor Practice is about advising clients on the law and handling legal matters, from contracts and disputes to property, corporate and family work. Solicitors research the law, draft documents, negotiate and guide clients through legal processes. Its purpose is to help people and organisations understand their rights and obligations and act on them safely.`,
  "Barrister & Advocacy": `Barrister and Advocacy is about giving specialist legal advice and representing clients in court, presenting arguments and advocating on their behalf. Barristers analyse cases, draft legal arguments and argue points of law before judges. Its purpose is to provide expert advocacy and opinion at the sharp end of the legal system, where cases are won and lost.`,
  "Private Equity & Venture Capital": `Private Equity and Venture Capital is about investing in companies to help them grow, from early stage startups to established businesses. Investors analyse deals, value companies, and support the businesses they back as they scale. Its purpose is to put capital and expertise behind companies with potential, aiming to build lasting value and strong returns.`,
  "Financial Analysis & FP&A": `Financial Analysis and FP&A is about analysing financial performance and planning to guide business decisions. Analysts build forecasts, budgets and models, and turn numbers into clear advice for managers and leaders. Its purpose is to help a business understand its own performance and plan its future with confidence.`,
  "Fintech & Digital Finance": `Fintech and Digital Finance is about building and improving the technology that powers modern finance, from payments and banking apps to digital investing and lending. Professionals work at the meeting point of finance and technology, on products, data and analysis. Its purpose is to make financial services faster, cheaper, more accessible and better designed than the traditional systems they replace.`,
  "Insurance & Actuarial": `Insurance and Actuarial is about measuring and managing risk, pricing insurance, and protecting people and organisations against uncertainty. Professionals use data, models and judgement to work out how likely events are and what they cost. Its purpose is to let individuals and businesses transfer risks they could not bear alone onto those who can pool and price them.`,
  "Journalism & Editorial": `Journalism and Editorial is about researching, writing and reporting stories and content for audiences across news and media. Journalists investigate, interview, write and edit, often to tight deadlines and high standards. Its purpose is to inform, explain and hold power to account, helping the public understand the world around them.`,
  "UX/UI Design": `UX and UI Design is the craft of shaping how people experience digital products, making apps, websites and services easy, useful and enjoyable to use. Designers research user needs, map journeys, build wireframes and prototypes, and design the clear, attractive interfaces people interact with. Its purpose is to bridge what a business wants to offer and what real people find intuitive, so technology actually works for the person using it.`,
  "Conservation & Land Management": `Conservation and Land Management is about protecting and managing nature, wildlife and landscapes, balancing the environment with how land is used. Practitioners survey habitats, manage sites, carry out fieldwork and advise on how to protect and restore nature. Its purpose is to keep ecosystems healthy and resilient in the face of development, climate change and biodiversity loss.`,
  "Data, Analytics & Quantitative Insight": `Data, Analytics & Quantitative Insight is a career world focused on using evidence, numbers, modelling, and structured thinking to understand problems and support better decisions. People in this world help organisations uncover patterns, predict outcomes, measure performance, reduce risk, and make sense of increasingly complex information.`,
  "Software, AI & Digital Systems": `Software, AI & Digital Systems is a career world centred around building the digital technologies that power modern life. People in this area create software, intelligent systems, digital platforms, and technical infrastructure that help individuals and organisations communicate, solve problems, automate processes, and interact with technology more effectively.`,
  "Engineering, Manufacturing & Infrastructure": `Engineering, Manufacturing & Infrastructure is a career world focused on designing, building, improving, and maintaining the physical systems and technologies that support modern society. People in this world help create everything from machines, transport systems, and energy networks to manufacturing processes, robotics, and large-scale infrastructure.`,
  "Architecture, Built Environment & Spatial Design": `Architecture, Built Environment & Spatial Design is a career world focused on shaping the places and spaces where people live, work, learn, travel, and connect. People in this world combine design imagination with practical planning, technical understanding, and awareness of how physical environments affect human behaviour and wellbeing.`,
  "Science, Research & Laboratory Innovation": `Science, Research & Laboratory Innovation is a career world focused on discovery, experimentation, and advancing human understanding through scientific investigation. People in this area help develop new knowledge, technologies, medicines, materials, and solutions that improve the way we understand and interact with the world.`,
  "Health Care & Clinical Practice": `Health Care & Clinical Practice is a career world centred around improving health, wellbeing, and quality of life through compassionate, evidence-informed care. People in this area work directly with individuals and communities to diagnose, treat, support, rehabilitate, and care for others across a wide range of clinical and healthcare settings.`,
  "Psychology, Behaviour & Human Insight": `Psychology, Behaviour & Human Insight is a career world focused on understanding how people think, feel, behave, learn, and develop. People in this area help improve wellbeing, relationships, decision-making, communication, and human performance across individuals, organisations, and society.`,
  "Education, Coaching & People Development": `Education, Coaching & People Development is a career world focused on helping people learn, grow, build confidence, and reach their potential. People in this area design, deliver, and support learning experiences across schools, early years settings, universities, workplaces, community organisations, and digital learning environments.`,
  "Law, Governance & Public Impact": `Law, Governance & Public Impact is a career world focused on rules, rights, accountability, public decision-making, and the systems that help societies function fairly. People in this world support legal processes, improve governance, analyse policy, manage risk, investigate wrongdoing, and help organisations act responsibly.`,
  "Business Strategy, Commercial & Leadership": `Business Strategy, Commercial & Leadership is a career world focused on helping organisations make better decisions, operate effectively, grow sustainably, and respond to change. People in this area connect ideas, people, processes, customers, partners, and resources so that organisations can deliver value and achieve their goals.`,
  "Finance, Economics & Investment": `Finance, Economics & Investment is a career world focused on understanding money, markets, value, risk, and how financial decisions shape organisations and economies. People in this area help individuals, businesses, investors, and institutions allocate resources, manage uncertainty, evaluate performance, and make informed financial choices.`,
  "Entrepreneurship, Innovation & Venture Building": `Entrepreneurship, Innovation & Venture Building is a career world focused on creating new ideas, building ventures, solving problems, and turning opportunities into real products, services, or organisations. People in this area often work in uncertain, fast-moving environments where they test ideas, attract support, build partnerships, and find practical ways to bring something new into the world.`,
  "Marketing, Media & Communication": `Marketing, Media & Communication is a career world focused on understanding audiences, shaping messages, building brands, and helping people connect with ideas, products, organisations, and causes. People in this area combine creativity, insight, storytelling, and strategy to influence how information is shared and how audiences respond.`,
  "Creative Arts, Design & Experience": `Creative Arts, Design & Experience is a career world centred around shaping how people experience products, brands, spaces, media, and digital environments. People in this world help turn ideas into experiences that are engaging, useful, visually compelling, and emotionally memorable. Their work influences how people interact with technology, communicate messages, connect with brands, and navigate both physical and digital spaces.`,
  "Environment, Sustainability & Planetary Futures": `Environment, Sustainability & Planetary Futures is a career world focused on protecting natural systems, reducing environmental harm, and helping organisations and societies transition towards more sustainable ways of living and working. People in this area use science, policy, strategy, data, and systems thinking to understand environmental challenges and design practical responses.`,
  "Society, Culture, Languages & Global Affairs": `Society, Culture, Languages & Global Affairs is a career world focused on understanding people, places, cultures, societies, and international relationships. People in this area help organisations and communities interpret social change, communicate across cultures, analyse global issues, and work with diverse groups and perspectives.`,
  "Core Data Analysis & Business Insight": `Core Data Analysis and Business Insight is about turning raw data into clear evidence that helps organisations understand performance and make better decisions. Analysts clean and analyse datasets, build reports, identify trends and translate findings into practical recommendations. Its purpose is to replace guesswork with evidence so teams and leaders can act with confidence.`,
  "Business Intelligence & Reporting": `Business Intelligence and Reporting is about building the dashboards, reports and measures that let an organisation see what is happening across its operations. Specialists connect data sources, track key indicators, visualise trends and make information easy for managers to use. Its purpose is to give the whole organisation a reliable, shared view of performance.`,
  "Customer & Market Insight": `Customer and Market Insight is about understanding customers, audiences, competitors and markets through research and data. Professionals combine surveys, behavioural data, interviews and market evidence to explain what people need, value and respond to. Its purpose is to give organisations a genuine understanding of the people and markets they serve, so decisions rest on reality rather than assumption.`,
  "Risk & Quantitative Analysis": `Risk and Quantitative Analysis uses statistical, financial and mathematical techniques to measure uncertainty and support decisions where accuracy really matters. Analysts model probability, pricing, exposure and future outcomes across insurance, banking, investment and operations. Its purpose is to put a credible number on risk so organisations can price it, hold capital against it and decide how much to take on.`,
  "Data Science & Advanced Modelling": `Data Science and Advanced Modelling uses statistics, programming and experimentation to explain complex patterns and predict future outcomes. Scientists build and test models, analyse large datasets, and turn advanced analysis into tools and recommendations that support decisions. Its purpose is to extract reliable, forward looking insight from data that is too large or complex for conventional analysis.`,
  "Machine Learning & Applied AI": `Machine Learning and Applied AI is about using data, models and algorithms to build systems that predict, classify, recommend or automate decisions. Practitioners prepare training data, evaluate model performance, test outputs and help organisations deploy intelligent systems responsibly. Its purpose is to put working AI into real products and processes, not just research.`,
  "Product, Growth & Experimentation Analytics": `Product, Growth and Experimentation Analytics uses data to improve digital products, user journeys and growth decisions. Analysts study product behaviour, run experiments, interpret conversion funnels and help teams decide what to build, test or improve next. Its purpose is to make product and growth decisions with evidence, so teams learn quickly what actually works.`,
  "Software Engineering": `Software Engineering is about designing, coding, testing and maintaining software applications and systems. Engineers build features, solve technical problems, review code and improve performance, usually as part of a team. Its purpose is to create the software that runs modern products, services and infrastructure, and to keep it working well.`,
  "Backend & Platform Engineering": `Backend and Platform Engineering focuses on the server side systems, APIs, databases, infrastructure and platforms that let digital products run reliably at scale. Engineers design system architecture, manage data and build the foundations other teams rely on. Its purpose is to make sure the systems behind an application are fast, reliable and able to grow.`,
  "Frontend & Web Development": `Frontend and Web Development focuses on building the parts of websites, apps and digital products that users see and interact with directly. Developers turn designs into responsive interfaces, improve usability and make experiences work across devices. Its purpose is to turn design and functionality into an interface that feels fast, clear and enjoyable to use.`,
  "Data Engineering": `Data Engineering is about building the pipelines, databases and platforms that let organisations collect, store, process and use data reliably. Engineers design data flows, manage infrastructure and make data available and trustworthy. Its purpose is to build the plumbing that everything else in data and AI depends on.`,
  "Quality Assurance & Test Engineering": `Quality Assurance and Test Engineering is about making sure software works correctly, safely and consistently before and after it reaches users. Engineers design test plans, automate checks, find bugs and safeguard quality. Its purpose is to catch problems before users do, so software can be trusted.`,
  "Cyber Security": `Cyber Security is about protecting digital systems, networks, data and users from threats, misuse and unauthorised access. Practitioners monitor risks, investigate incidents, test vulnerabilities and strengthen defences. Its purpose is to keep organisations and people safe in a world where almost everything depends on digital systems under constant attack.`,
  "AI & Machine Learning Engineering": `AI and Machine Learning Engineering focuses on turning AI models into working systems, products and services. Engineers build model pipelines, deploy machine learning solutions, monitor performance and integrate AI into real applications. Its purpose is to make artificial intelligence actually work in production, reliably and safely, not just in research.`,
  "Mechanical Design & Development Engineering": `Mechanical Design and Development Engineering is about designing, testing and improving mechanical products, components and systems. Engineers apply engineering principles, CAD, prototyping, simulation and testing to develop physical solutions across manufacturing, transport, energy, aerospace and consumer products. Its purpose is to turn ideas and requirements into mechanical things that work reliably in the real world.`,
  "Electrical & Electronic Engineering": `Electrical and Electronic Engineering focuses on electrical systems, circuits, electronics, control, sensors, power and connected technologies. Engineers design, test, troubleshoot and improve the hardware and electrical systems behind products, infrastructure, automation, communications and energy networks. Its purpose is to make the electrical and electronic systems that modern life and industry run on work reliably.`,
  "Manufacturing & Production Engineering": `Manufacturing and Production Engineering is about how products are made efficiently, safely, consistently and at scale. Engineers improve production methods, quality, equipment, workflow and process reliability across factories and advanced manufacturing environments. Its purpose is to turn designs into products that can be made well, again and again, at the right cost and quality.`,
  "Process & Industrial Engineering": `Process and Industrial Engineering is about improving systems, workflows and operations so organisations deliver better results with less waste. Engineers analyse bottlenecks, redesign processes, optimise resources and use data to improve productivity, quality and efficiency. Its purpose is to make how work gets done faster, cheaper and more reliable without cutting corners.`,
  "Systems Engineering": `Systems Engineering is about designing and integrating complex systems where many technical parts must work together reliably. Engineers define requirements, coordinate components, manage interfaces, test performance and ensure the whole system functions as intended. Its purpose is to keep sight of the whole when a system is too large and interconnected for any one discipline to hold alone.`,
  "Robotics & Automation Engineering": `Robotics and Automation Engineering is about designing, programming, testing and improving robotic and automated systems. Engineers combine sensors, control, mechanical design and software to automate tasks, improve precision and support safer, more efficient operations. Its purpose is to build machines and systems that carry out physical work reliably, often where it is repetitive, precise or dangerous for people.`,
  "Civil & Structural Engineering": `Civil and Structural Engineering is about designing, analysing and delivering infrastructure such as buildings, bridges, roads, foundations and drainage. Engineers assess safety, materials, loads and site conditions to create reliable, lasting built assets. Its purpose is to provide the physical foundations of society, the structures and networks that everyday life depends on.`,
  "Infrastructure, Maintenance & Asset Engineering": `Infrastructure, Maintenance and Asset Engineering is about keeping engineering assets, infrastructure and equipment safe, reliable and cost effective over their whole life. Engineers plan maintenance, monitor performance, manage asset lifecycles and reduce downtime. Its purpose is to make sure critical systems keep working dependably long after they are first built.`,
  "Architecture": `Architecture is the design of buildings and spaces that have to work as pieces of creativity, engineering and everyday human experience at once. Architects develop concepts, produce drawings and models, and coordinate with engineers, clients and planners to turn ideas into something that can actually be built. Its purpose is to shape the places people live, work and move through, balancing design quality against cost, regulation and sustainability.`,
  "Town Planning & Urban Development": `Town Planning and Urban Development is the discipline of deciding how towns, cities and regions should grow and change over time. Planners weigh up housing need, transport, land use, environmental impact and policy to shape where and how development happens. Its purpose is to help places develop in a way that is workable, fair and sustainable for the communities who live in them.`,
  "Architectural Technology & BIM": `Architectural Technology and BIM is the technical backbone of building design, turning architectural intent into accurate, coordinated, buildable information. Specialists produce detailed drawings and digital models, apply building standards and materials knowledge, and make sure a design works when it reaches site. Its purpose is to close the gap between a design idea and a building that can be constructed safely and efficiently.`,
  "Construction Project Delivery": `Construction Project Delivery is the management of building and infrastructure projects so they are completed safely, on time, on budget and to the required quality. Delivery professionals coordinate contractors, programmes, budgets, risk and safety across the life of a project. Its purpose is to turn designs and plans into finished, functioning places while keeping a complex web of people and constraints under control.`,
  "Surveying & Cost Consultancy": `Surveying and Cost Consultancy covers the measurement, cost, value and commercial management of buildings and construction projects. Surveyors estimate and control costs, assess the condition and value of property, advise on contracts, and help clients make sound property and construction decisions. Its purpose is to protect value and manage risk in some of the largest financial commitments organisations make.`,
  "Sustainability & Building Performance": `Sustainability and Building Performance is about improving how buildings use energy, materials and resources across their whole life. Specialists assess environmental performance, advise on low carbon design, model and analyse building data, and help projects meet sustainability and wellbeing targets. Its purpose is to reduce the environmental footprint of the built environment while making buildings healthier and cheaper to run.`,
  "Laboratory Science": `Laboratory Science is about carrying out controlled tests, experiments and analyses in laboratory settings. Practitioners prepare samples, follow protocols, operate scientific equipment and record results accurately. Its purpose is to produce the reliable measurements and results that research, industry and healthcare depend on.`,
  "R&D Science": `R&D Science is about developing new knowledge, products, materials, processes and technologies through research and experimentation. Practitioners design studies, test hypotheses, analyse results and refine prototypes. Its purpose is to push the boundaries of what is known or possible and turn discovery into things that work.`,
  "Materials & Chemical Analysis": `Materials and Chemical Analysis is about testing, characterising and improving chemicals, materials, compounds and substances. Practitioners use analytical techniques, laboratory equipment and quality standards to understand what things are made of and how they behave. Its purpose is to give industry and research reliable knowledge of materials, so products are safe, effective and fit for purpose.`,
  "Biomedical & Clinical Research": `Biomedical and Clinical Research is about understanding disease, treatment and human biology through scientific study and clinical evidence. Practitioners support studies, analyse biological or patient data and help run research. Its purpose is to advance understanding of health and disease and to move discoveries toward better treatments.`,
  "Scientific Data & Bioinformatics": `Scientific Data and Bioinformatics is about using computational tools, statistics and scientific datasets to answer research questions. Practitioners analyse genomic, biomedical, environmental and experimental data to find patterns and meaning. Its purpose is to make sense of the huge, complex datasets that modern science now produces.`,
  "Clinical Trials & Translational Research": `Clinical Trials and Translational Research is about moving scientific discoveries toward practical healthcare use through trials, evidence generation and applied research. Practitioners coordinate studies, manage data and help bridge the lab and the clinic. Its purpose is to turn promising science into treatments that are proven safe and effective in real patients.`,
  "Clinical Medicine / Doctor": `Clinical Medicine is about diagnosing illness, treating patients, managing care and making evidence based decisions in hospitals, GP practices and specialist services. Doctors combine medical knowledge, communication and investigation to work out what is wrong and what to do. Its purpose is to understand and treat illness in individual patients, guiding them through some of the most important moments of their lives.`,
  "Surgery & Procedural Medicine": `Surgery and Procedural Medicine is about treating disease, injury and physical conditions through operations, procedures and highly technical clinical interventions. Practitioners assess patients, plan procedures and operate with precision, then oversee recovery. Its purpose is to physically correct or remove what is causing harm, often in ways nothing else can achieve.`,
  "Acute, Emergency & Critical Care": `Acute, Emergency and Critical Care is about responding to urgent, complex and high risk health situations where rapid assessment and decision making are essential. Practitioners stabilise patients, manage emergencies and interpret clinical signs fast. Its purpose is to keep the sickest and most urgent patients alive and stable when time is critical.`,
  "Mental Health & Behavioural Medicine": `Mental Health and Behavioural Medicine is about diagnosing, treating and supporting people experiencing mental health, behavioural, emotional or psychiatric difficulties. Practitioners combine medical knowledge, psychological understanding and therapeutic skill. Its purpose is to help people recover, manage and live well with conditions that affect the mind and behaviour.`,
  "Diagnostic & Investigative Medicine": `Diagnostic and Investigative Medicine is about identifying disease and guiding treatment through imaging, pathology, genetics, microbiology and other specialist investigations. Practitioners interpret evidence, run or review tests and reach the conclusions that direct care. Its purpose is to work out exactly what is wrong so that treatment can be targeted correctly.`,
  "Public Health Medicine, Epidemiology & Health Policy": `Public Health Medicine, Epidemiology and Health Policy is about improving health at population level rather than treating one patient at a time. Practitioners analyse disease patterns, design prevention strategies and advise on policy. Its purpose is to protect and improve the health of whole communities and to reduce inequalities in who gets ill and why.`,
  "Academic Medicine & Clinical Research": `Academic Medicine and Clinical Research combines clinical knowledge with research, teaching and innovation. Practitioners investigate medical questions, contribute to trials and studies, teach future professionals and help generate the evidence that improves care. Its purpose is to advance medicine itself, turning research into better treatment and training the clinicians who deliver it.`,
  "Healthcare Leadership & Service Improvement": `Healthcare Leadership and Service Improvement is about improving how healthcare services are organised, delivered, measured and experienced. Practitioners work on quality improvement, patient safety, service redesign and operations. Its purpose is to help health services do more good for more people, more safely and efficiently, with the resources they have.`,
  "Digital Health, Healthtech & Medical Innovation": `Digital Health, Healthtech and Medical Innovation is about using technology, data, AI and product innovation to improve healthcare delivery and patient outcomes. Practitioners help design, evaluate, implement and advise on digital tools and new models of care. Its purpose is to bring the pace and power of technology to a health system that badly needs it, without losing sight of safety and evidence.`,
  "Nursing": `Nursing is about delivering safe, compassionate and evidence informed care across hospitals, communities, mental health, children's and specialist services. Nurses assess needs, monitor patients, provide treatment and coordinate much of the care around them. Its purpose is to care for people through illness, recovery and vulnerability, and to be the constant presence in a patient's experience of healthcare.`,
  "Public Health Nursing & Health Visiting": `Public Health Nursing and Health Visiting is about prevention, family health, child development and community wellbeing. Practitioners work with families, children and communities to identify needs early, reduce risk and support healthy development. Its purpose is to protect and improve health before problems become serious, especially for children and families who need extra support.`,
  "Clinical Research Nursing": `Clinical Research Nursing combines patient care with the delivery of clinical studies and trials. Practitioners support participants, collect accurate data, follow research protocols and help generate the evidence behind new treatments. Its purpose is to make medical research happen safely and rigorously, with the patient's wellbeing at the centre.`,
  "Nurse Education & Leadership": `Nurse Education and Leadership is about developing nursing practice, supporting teams, improving care quality and helping other professionals learn. Practitioners supervise staff, design training, lead services and support clinical development. Its purpose is to raise the standard of care across a team or organisation by developing the people who deliver it.`,
  "Midwifery": `Midwifery is about supporting women, babies and families through pregnancy, birth and the early weeks afterwards. Midwives provide clinical care, emotional support, health education and safe decision making, and know when to escalate. Its purpose is to guide families safely through one of life's most significant experiences, protecting the health of mother and baby.`,
  "Rehabilitation & Functional Independence": `Rehabilitation and Functional Independence is about helping people recover movement, function, confidence and independence after illness, injury, disability or long term health challenges. Practitioners assess abilities, design therapy and support people to regain what they can. Its purpose is to help people live as fully and independently as possible, whatever their condition.`,
  "Clinical Science & Laboratory Diagnostics": `Clinical Science and Laboratory Diagnostics is about using scientific testing and interpretation to support diagnosis, treatment and disease monitoring. Practitioners analyse samples, operate specialist equipment, validate results and advise clinicians. Its purpose is to provide the accurate laboratory evidence that underpins a huge share of medical decisions.`,
  "Diagnostics, Imaging & Clinical Support (Legacy Unrouted)": `Diagnostics, Imaging and Clinical Support focuses on producing and interpreting the clinical images and technical evidence that help diagnose and monitor health conditions. Practitioners use regulated equipment and patient facing skills to capture accurate results. Its purpose is to give clinical teams the reliable evidence they need to make the right decisions.`,
  "Pharmacy (Legacy Broad Route)": `Pharmacy focuses on medicines, therapeutics, safety and patient advice. Pharmacists understand how medicines work, support safe prescribing and dispensing, and advise patients and clinicians. Its purpose is to make sure medicines are used safely, effectively and to best effect for each patient.`,
  "Paramedic Practice & Emergency Care": `Paramedic Practice and Emergency Care is about responding to urgent health situations outside hospital and making rapid decisions in unpredictable environments. Paramedics assess patients, provide emergency treatment and manage the journey to further care. Its purpose is to bring skilled emergency care to people wherever they are, in the crucial first minutes and hours.`,
  "Emergency Planning & Ambulance Service Leadership": `Emergency Planning and Ambulance Service Leadership is about organising urgent care systems, emergency response capacity and resilience planning. Practitioners coordinate services, plan for incidents and improve operations. Its purpose is to make sure that when emergencies happen, the system is ready to respond quickly, safely and at scale.`,
  "Public Health & Health Improvement": `Public Health and Health Improvement is about preventing illness, reducing inequalities and improving health across communities. Practitioners design campaigns, analyse population needs and support local services and partnerships. Its purpose is to help whole communities live healthier lives and to close the gaps in health between different groups.`,
  "Healthcare Operations & Service Improvement": `Healthcare Operations and Service Improvement is about making healthcare services safer, smoother, more efficient and more responsive to patients. Practitioners analyse service data, redesign processes and coordinate the practical delivery of care. Its purpose is to keep complex health services running well so that patients get timely, reliable care.`,
  "Social Work & Safeguarding": `Social Work and Safeguarding is about protecting vulnerable people, assessing needs and risks, and helping individuals and families access the right support. Practitioners work across care, health, education and justice to keep people safe and help them cope. Its purpose is to protect and support people at the most difficult and risky points in their lives.`,
  "Dentistry / Dentist": `Dentistry is about oral health, diagnosis, prevention, treatment planning and clinical procedures for the teeth, gums and wider mouth. Dentists combine precision, patient care, technical skill and health education. Its purpose is to keep people's mouths healthy and pain free and to restore function and appearance when problems arise.`,
  "Specialist Dentistry": `Specialist Dentistry is advanced dental practice in areas such as orthodontics, oral surgery, restorative or paediatric dentistry. Specialists handle more complex cases, use advanced techniques and provide expertise beyond general practice. Its purpose is to treat the difficult, complex or specialised problems that need deeper training and skill.`,
  "Dental Research & Academic Dentistry": `Dental Research and Academic Dentistry combines dental knowledge with scientific research, teaching and innovation. Practitioners investigate oral health questions, evaluate treatments, teach future dentists and generate evidence. Its purpose is to advance dental science and practice and to train the profession's next generation.`,
  "Oral Health Policy & Dental Public Health": `Oral Health Policy and Dental Public Health is about improving oral health at population level through prevention, service planning, access and policy. Practitioners analyse needs, design interventions and support fairer access to dental care. Its purpose is to improve the nation's oral health and to reduce the inequalities in who suffers dental disease.`,
  "Clinical Pharmacy": `Clinical Pharmacy is about optimising medicines for individual patients in hospitals, clinics, GP practices and specialist services. Pharmacists review prescriptions, advise clinical teams, monitor safety and support treatment decisions. Its purpose is to make sure each patient gets the safest, most effective medicines for their situation.`,
  "Community Pharmacy": `Community Pharmacy is about accessible medicines advice, dispensing, public health support and patient facing services in local communities. Pharmacists advise patients, manage prescriptions and provide services such as vaccinations and health checks. Its purpose is to be the accessible, everyday face of healthcare on the high street, close to where people live.`,
  "Pharmaceutical Industry & Drug Development": `Pharmaceutical Industry and Drug Development is about creating, testing, regulating and bringing medicines and therapies to market. Professionals work across research, clinical trials, medical affairs and product development. Its purpose is to turn scientific discovery into safe, effective treatments that reach the patients who need them.`,
  "Regulatory Affairs & Medicines Safety": `Regulatory Affairs and Medicines Safety is about making sure medicines, devices and health products meet safety, quality, legal and evidence requirements. Professionals prepare submissions, monitor adverse events and manage compliance. Its purpose is to protect patients by ensuring that only safe, effective, well evidenced products reach and stay on the market.`,
  "Medicines Policy & Public Health Pharmacy": `Medicines Policy and Public Health Pharmacy is about how medicines are used safely, fairly and effectively across populations and health systems. Professionals work on formularies, access, prescribing policy and public health programmes. Its purpose is to make sure whole populations get good value, safe and equitable access to the medicines they need.`,
  "Clinical Psychology & Mental Health Support": `Clinical Psychology and Mental Health Support is about understanding psychological distress, behaviour, emotional wellbeing and mental health needs. Practitioners support assessment, formulation, intervention and recovery. Its purpose is to help people understand and overcome psychological difficulties and to improve their mental health and wellbeing.`,
  "Counselling, Psychotherapy & Therapeutic Practice": `Counselling and Psychotherapy is about providing structured therapeutic support for people experiencing emotional, relational or psychological difficulties. Practitioners build safe helping relationships, explore patterns and support change. Its purpose is to give people a confidential, skilled space to work through what troubles them and to grow.`,
  "Learning, Development & Behaviour Support": `Learning, Development and Behaviour Support is about helping children, young people and learners overcome barriers to learning, behaviour, confidence and development. Practitioners support assessment, intervention, mentoring and targeted help. Its purpose is to help young people who are struggling to learn and thrive to get back on track.`,
  "People Analytics & Workplace Behaviour": `People Analytics and Workplace Behaviour is about understanding employee behaviour, performance, engagement, wellbeing and culture through data and behavioural insight. Practitioners analyse workforce patterns and translate them into better people decisions. Its purpose is to bring evidence and rigour to how organisations understand and manage their people.`,
  "UX Research & Behavioural Insight": `UX Research and Behavioural Insight is about understanding how people think, decide, feel and interact with products, services and systems. Practitioners run research, analyse behaviour, test designs and translate human insight into better experiences. Its purpose is to make sure products and services are designed around how people actually behave, not how designers assume they do.`,
  "Justice, Rehabilitation & Behaviour Change": `Justice, Rehabilitation and Behaviour Change is about understanding risk, behaviour, rehabilitation and support within justice and safeguarding contexts. Practitioners assess needs, support behaviour change and manage risk. Its purpose is to reduce harm and reoffending and to help people in the justice system turn their lives around.`,
  "Primary Teaching & Classroom Practice": `Primary Teaching is about planning, teaching and supporting learning for children across the whole primary curriculum. Teachers create lessons, manage classrooms, assess progress and build the relationships that help pupils develop academically, socially and emotionally. Its purpose is to give children a strong, confident start that shapes how they learn for the rest of their lives.`,
  "Early Years & Family Support": `Early Years and Family Support focuses on children's development, learning and wellbeing in the earliest years, and on supporting the families around them. Practitioners create safe, stimulating environments, support communication and social development, spot needs early and work with families and services. Its purpose is to give young children the secure, enriching start that shapes their whole development.`,
  "SEND & Inclusion Support": `SEND and Inclusion Support is about helping learners with special educational needs, disabilities or additional barriers to access education and thrive. Practitioners adapt learning, provide targeted support, coordinate with other professionals and promote inclusion and confidence. Its purpose is to make sure every learner, whatever their needs, can take part and make progress.`,
  "Learning Design & Educational Technology": `Learning Design and Educational Technology is about designing learning experiences, resources, courses and digital tools that help people learn effectively. Practitioners combine pedagogy, content design, technology, creativity and evaluation. Its purpose is to make learning clearer, more engaging and more accessible, whether in a classroom, a workplace or online.`,
  "Training, Learning & Development": `Training, Learning and Development is about building skills and capability inside workplaces and organisations. Practitioners design workshops, learning programmes, onboarding and coaching that help employees perform and grow. Its purpose is to make sure people and organisations keep developing the skills they need as work changes.`,
  "Education Support, Outreach & Student Services": `Education Support, Outreach and Student Services is about helping learners access opportunities, navigate education and get the right practical and pastoral support. Practitioners coordinate services, advise students, run outreach and support progression. Its purpose is to remove the barriers around learning so more people can take part and succeed, especially those least likely to.`,
  "Legal Support & Casework": `Legal Support and Casework is about supporting legal processes by preparing documents, researching cases, managing evidence and helping clients and organisations navigate legal issues. Practitioners work alongside solicitors and legal teams to keep cases moving. Its purpose is to do the essential groundwork that makes legal cases run accurately and efficiently.`,
  "Governance, Risk & Compliance": `Governance, Risk and Compliance is about helping organisations follow the rules, manage risk, maintain controls and act responsibly. Practitioners monitor regulation, review policies, assess compliance and document decisions. Its purpose is to keep organisations safe, ethical and within the law as regulation grows more complex.`,
  "Public Affairs & Advocacy": `Public Affairs and Advocacy is about influencing decisions, representing interests and communicating with policymakers, stakeholders and the public. Practitioners monitor policy, build relationships and prepare arguments and campaigns. Its purpose is to give organisations and causes a voice in the decisions that affect them, and to shape policy through persuasion.`,
  "Investigations & Financial Crime": `Investigations and Financial Crime is about identifying misconduct, fraud, money laundering, regulatory breaches and suspicious activity. Practitioners analyse evidence, review transactions, prepare reports and interview those involved. Its purpose is to detect and stop wrongdoing and to protect organisations, markets and the public from financial crime.`,
  "Policy & Public Sector Analysis": `Policy and Public Sector Analysis is about researching social, economic and public problems and developing evidence based recommendations. Practitioners analyse data, consult stakeholders, write briefings and support decisions. Its purpose is to help government and public bodies make better informed choices about issues that affect society.`,
  "Generalist Business Programmes": `Generalist Business Programmes give broad exposure across an organisation, from operations and finance to marketing, strategy and commercial teams. Participants rotate through functions, learn how a business works from several angles, and build the foundations for future management. Their purpose is to develop well rounded people who understand the whole organisation before specialising or moving into leadership.`,
  "Operations & Supply Chain": `Operations and Supply Chain is about how goods, services, information and resources move through an organisation. Professionals analyse workflows, coordinate suppliers, manage capacity, cut waste and keep delivery efficient and reliable at scale. Its purpose is to make sure what a business promises actually reaches customers on time, at quality and at a sensible cost.`,
  "Business Analysis": `Business Analysis is the discipline of understanding an organisation's problems, processes and needs so teams can improve systems, services and ways of working. Analysts gather evidence, map workflows, identify gaps and translate business needs into clear, practical requirements. Its purpose is to make sure that changes and new systems solve the right problem in the right way.`,
  "Project, PMO & Transformation": `Project, PMO and Transformation is about planning, coordinating and delivering organisational change. Professionals manage timelines, governance, risk, budgets and stakeholder communication so complex initiatives move from idea to implementation. Its purpose is to give big, messy changes the structure and momentum they need to actually land.`,
  "Consulting & Strategic Improvement": `Consulting and Strategic Improvement is about helping organisations diagnose problems, find opportunities and make better strategic decisions. Consultants structure problems, analyse evidence, develop recommendations and support change across strategy, operations, technology and people. Its purpose is to bring outside rigour and fresh thinking to the decisions an organisation cannot easily make on its own.`,
  "Business Development & Commercial Partnerships": `Business Development and Strategic Partnerships is about creating growth through new relationships, markets and commercial opportunities. Professionals find prospects, build partnerships, understand customer needs and negotiate deals that open new avenues for the organisation. Its purpose is to expand where and how a business can grow by forging valuable external relationships.`,
  "HR, People & Organisations": `HR, People and Organisations is about how organisations attract, develop, support and retain their people. Professionals shape recruitment, employee experience, learning, performance, culture and organisational change. Its purpose is to help both people and the organisation thrive, aligning what employees need with what the business is trying to do.`,
  "Investment Banking & Corporate Finance": `Investment Banking and Corporate Finance focuses on major financial decisions such as mergers and acquisitions, raising capital, valuations and restructuring. Professionals analyse companies, build financial models, prepare deal materials and support clients through high stakes transactions. Its purpose is to advise organisations on the biggest financial decisions they make and to move large amounts of capital where it is needed.`,
  "Equity Research & Investment Research": `Equity Research and Investment Research is about analysing companies, sectors and markets to support investment decisions. Analysts build valuation models, read financial statements, assess strategy and risk, and produce recommendations and investment views. Its purpose is to form a well evidenced opinion on what an investment is really worth and whether it is a good idea.`,
  "Asset & Wealth Management": `Asset and Wealth Management is about managing investments for individuals, institutions, pension funds and other clients with long term goals. Professionals analyse portfolios and markets, support investment decisions, and help grow and protect wealth. Its purpose is to steward other people's money responsibly toward their financial goals over years and decades.`,
  "Commercial & Corporate Banking": `Commercial and Corporate Banking is about providing lending, cash management and financial services to businesses and larger organisations. Professionals assess credit, analyse company performance, manage client relationships and structure banking solutions. Its purpose is to provide the funding and financial services that let businesses operate, invest and grow.`,
  "Markets & Trading": `Markets and Trading is about analysing, buying, selling and managing financial instruments such as shares, currencies, commodities, bonds and derivatives across global markets. Professionals interpret market movements, assess risk and make rapid decisions based on data, events and market behaviour. Its purpose is to price risk and provide liquidity in the markets the wider financial system relies on.`,
  "Treasury & Liquidity": `Treasury and Liquidity is about managing an organisation's cash, funding, liquidity and financial risk. Professionals monitor cash flows, manage funding needs, support hedging decisions and help ensure the organisation can meet its obligations. Its purpose is to keep an organisation financially secure, with the cash and funding it needs to operate whatever happens.`,
  "Risk, Compliance & Controls": `Risk, Compliance and Controls is about identifying, measuring and managing financial, operational, regulatory and conduct risks. Professionals test controls, review processes, analyse exposure, support audits and help organisations operate safely and within the rules. Its purpose is to protect an organisation and its customers from harm and to keep it on the right side of regulation.`,
  "Banking Operations & Middle Office": `Banking Operations and Middle Office is about the processes, controls, data and trade support that keep financial services running accurately behind the scenes. Professionals reconcile transactions, monitor controls, support the trade lifecycle and manage operational risk. Its purpose is to make sure that what the front office agrees is settled, recorded and controlled correctly, every time.`,
  "Accounting, Audit & Assurance": `Accounting, Audit and Assurance is about financial records, reporting, controls and the independent review of organisational information. Professionals prepare accounts, test evidence, review financial statements, assess controls and help stakeholders trust financial information. Its purpose is to make sure financial information is accurate and reliable, which the whole economy depends on.`,
  "Sustainable Finance & Impact Investing": `Sustainable Finance and Impact Investing is about directing capital toward organisations and projects that consider environmental, social and governance outcomes alongside financial returns. Professionals analyse ESG data, assess impact, evaluate risks and support responsible investment decisions. Its purpose is to use the power of finance to drive positive change while still delivering sound returns.`,
  "Venture Building & Founder": `Venture Building and Founder is about creating, testing and growing new businesses, products or services from early stage ideas. Founders identify unmet needs, validate opportunities, build teams and resources, and adapt fast in uncertain conditions. Its purpose is to turn an idea into a real, viable venture, and to carry the risk and ownership of doing so.`,
  "Start-up Operations": `Startup Operations is about making an early stage venture work day to day and scale effectively. Professionals build processes, coordinate teams, solve practical problems and manage the internal systems that keep a fast moving company running. Its purpose is to turn a founder's fast moving ideas into organised, repeatable execution.`,
  "Product Growth & Business Development in Start-ups": `Product Growth and Business Development in Startups is about improving what a venture offers and how quickly it reaches customers and finds early traction. Professionals test ideas, analyse user behaviour, run experiments and pursue the partnerships and channels that drive growth. Its purpose is to help a young venture find and accelerate the things that actually make it grow.`,
  "Venture Capital, Accelerators & Innovation Support": `Venture Capital, Accelerators and Innovation Support is about helping start ups develop, raise investment and grow. Professionals assess ventures, analyse markets, support founders, run programmes and connect new businesses with funding, expertise and networks. Its purpose is to identify promising ventures and give them the capital and support they need to succeed.`,
  "Brand & Marketing Strategy": `Brand and Marketing Strategy is about defining how an organisation, product or service should be positioned, understood and remembered by its audience. Strategists analyse customers, competitors and trends and shape messaging and identity. Its purpose is to give a brand a clear, distinctive place in people's minds and to guide how it grows.`,
  "Performance Marketing & Growth": `Performance Marketing and Growth is about measurable marketing designed to attract, convert and retain customers. Practitioners run digital campaigns, analyse conversion data, test channels and optimise spend. Its purpose is to grow a business efficiently by finding, proving and scaling the marketing that actually works.`,
  "PR & Communications": `PR and Communications is about reputation, messaging, media relationships and public understanding. Practitioners write content, prepare statements, manage campaigns and handle press and stakeholder activity. Its purpose is to shape how an organisation is understood and to protect and build its reputation, especially when it matters most.`,
  "Market Research & Audience Insight": `Market Research and Audience Insight is about understanding audiences, markets, competitors and behaviour through evidence. Practitioners design research, analyse survey and interview data, interpret trends and help organisations understand their customers. Its purpose is to replace guesswork about what people want with real, usable evidence.`,
  "Content & Social Media": `Content and Social Media is about creating, publishing and managing messages across digital channels to engage audiences. Practitioners develop posts, videos, campaigns, editorial plans and community content. Its purpose is to build and hold an audience's attention and connection in a crowded, fast moving digital world.`,
  "Product & Industrial Design": `Product and Industrial Design is the design of physical products, from consumer goods and tools to equipment and everyday objects, so they are useful, usable and possible to manufacture. Designers research users, sketch and prototype concepts, test materials, and refine designs toward production. Its purpose is to turn ideas into well made objects that work in people's hands and can be built at scale.`,
  "Graphic Design & Visual Communication": `Graphic Design and Visual Communication turns ideas, information and messages into clear, compelling visual form. Designers create layouts, brand identities, campaigns, illustration, packaging and digital assets that communicate meaning quickly and memorably. Its purpose is to help organisations and audiences understand and feel something through visual language.`,
  "Animation & Motion Design": `Animation and Motion Design is the creation of movement and visual storytelling for film, games, advertising, education, interfaces and social media. Designers develop storyboards, animate characters or graphics, edit sequences and bring ideas to life through motion. Its purpose is to communicate and entertain by giving still ideas time, rhythm and emotion.`,
  "Digital Design & Multimedia": `Digital Design and Multimedia is the creation of visual and interactive content across websites, apps, campaigns, screens and digital platforms. Designers combine design, media production and digital tools to build engaging online experiences. Its purpose is to help brands, products and audiences connect through content that works fluently across many digital channels.`,
  "Environmental Science & Monitoring": `Environmental Science and Monitoring is about measuring, assessing and interpreting environmental conditions such as air, water, land, biodiversity and pollution. Scientists collect data, conduct fieldwork, prepare reports and support evidence based environmental decisions. Its purpose is to give society reliable evidence about the state of the environment so it can be protected and managed well.`,
  "Sustainability & ESG Advisory": `Sustainability and ESG Advisory is about helping organisations understand, measure, report and improve their environmental, social and governance performance. Advisers analyse data, advise on targets, prepare disclosures and support strategy. Its purpose is to help organisations meet rising expectations from regulators, investors and society, and to make sustainability part of how they actually operate.`,
  "Circular Economy & Sustainable Supply Chains": `Circular Economy and Sustainable Supply Chains is about reducing waste, improving resource use and making products, materials and supply networks more sustainable. Practitioners analyse supply chains, redesign processes, assess suppliers and support circular or low impact business models. Its purpose is to move production and consumption away from a take, make and dispose model toward one that keeps materials in use.`,
  "Environmental Policy & Impact Assessment": `Environmental Policy and Impact Assessment is about understanding how projects, policies and developments affect the environment and communities. Practitioners assess risks, prepare impact reports, interpret regulation, consult stakeholders and support better planning decisions. Its purpose is to make sure environmental and social consequences are properly weighed before decisions are made.`,
  "Net Zero, Climate & Sustainability Strategy": `Net Zero, Climate and Sustainability Strategy is about helping organisations reduce emissions, manage climate risk and plan long term sustainability transitions. Strategists analyse carbon data, develop roadmaps, advise on targets and support strategic change. Its purpose is to turn climate ambition into credible plans that reshape how organisations operate over the coming decades.`,
  "International Relations, Policy & Geopolitical Analysis": `International Relations, Policy and Geopolitical Analysis is about understanding global politics, institutions, conflict, trade, security and international decision making. Practitioners analyse events, produce assessments and advise on strategy and policy. Its purpose is to make sense of a complex, interconnected world so that organisations and governments can act wisely within it.`,
  "Languages, Translation & Localisation": `Languages, Translation and Localisation is about helping messages, products, services and content work across languages and cultures. Practitioners translate, adapt, edit, interpret and localise communication so it lands naturally with different audiences. Its purpose is to let ideas, businesses and people communicate across the barriers of language and culture.`,
  "International Development & NGO Programmes": `International Development and NGO Programmes is about improving social, economic, health, education and humanitarian outcomes across communities and countries. Practitioners coordinate programmes, monitor impact and work with partners and communities. Its purpose is to tackle poverty, inequality and crisis, and to help communities build better lives.`,
  "Social Research & Cultural Analysis": `Social Research and Cultural Analysis is about understanding societies, communities, identities, behaviour and cultural change through research. Practitioners collect and analyse qualitative and quantitative evidence to explain how people live and why. Its purpose is to build reliable understanding of social life that can inform policy, organisations and public debate.`,
  "Intelligence, Public Service & Security Analysis": `Intelligence, Public Service and Security Analysis is about interpreting information that supports public safety, national interests, policy and operational decisions. Practitioners analyse evidence, assess risk and produce assessments for decision makers. Its purpose is to give those who protect the public and the nation a clear, objective understanding of threats and events.`,
